# Security, RBAC & audit

## Source of truth
- Permission **codes**: `src/lib/permissions.ts` (`PERMISSIONS`, `DEFAULT_ROLE_PERMISSIONS`)
- Permission **labels / groups**: `src/lib/permission-catalog.ts` (`PERMISSION_CATALOG`)
- Role guide copy: `src/config/roles.ts` — `ROLE_CATALOG.permissions` **must** mirror `DEFAULT_ROLE_PERMISSIONS`
- Live grants: DB `RolePermission` (edited under Admin → Roles & Access)
- Opening the RBAC matrix upserts any missing catalog permissions into DB

## Roles and core permissions
| Role | Core permissions | Restrictions |
|---|---|---|
| Design Head | Create/approve concepts, assign/reassign, stage tasks, cost/time, corrections, workflow override | Cannot alter server time events directly |
| Sketch Designer | Assigned sketch tasks, timers, corrections | No final approval or KPI weight editing |
| Punching Designer | Punching tasks, EMB/DST, corrections | No concept deletion after approval |
| Machine Operator | Sample / machine tasks | No design-level approval |
| Sample Checker | Checklist, approve/reject/re-sample, corrections, `DESIGN_APPROVE` | No cost master changes |
| Costing Team | Cost entries + `ERP_ACCOUNTS_OPERATE` | No design create / final approve |
| Production Head | Production release, floor + sales ERP | No admin masters |
| Admin | All permissions incl. `MASTER_ADMIN` | All admin actions audited |
| Management/Owner | Approve, KPI, team time, production release, full ERP SoD | No process master configuration |

## Permission codes (full)
`DESIGN_CREATE`, `DESIGN_ASSIGN`, `TASK_EXECUTE`, `TIME_VIEW_TEAM`,
`CORRECTION_RAISE`, `DESIGN_APPROVE`, `COST_VIEW`, `KPI_ADMIN`,
`MASTER_ADMIN`, `PRODUCTION_RELEASE`, `WORKFLOW_OVERRIDE`,
`ERP_FLOOR_OPERATE`, `ERP_SALES_OPERATE`, `ERP_ACCOUNTS_OPERATE`.

## Roles & Access UX
Stepwise: **1 People & roles** (user names) → **2 Permissions** (permission column × roles, grouped) → **3 Role guide**.

## Rules
- Authenticated identity on every API call; never accept `CreatedBy`/
  `EmployeeId` from the client when it can be derived from the token.
- Object-level authorization: validate `DesignId`/`TaskId` against the
  caller's role and org/company/location scope on every request.
- Sensitive cost/KPI screens require extra permissions beyond basic design access.
- Audit: design edits, task state changes, reassignment, correction
  responsibility, approval, cost changes, KPI definition changes, file deletion,
  role permission updates.
- Never expose physical server file paths in API responses; use signed,
  non-guessable download URLs for confidential design files.
- Apply anti-malware/file-scanning policy to uploads where infrastructure supports it.
- When adding a permission: update `PERMISSIONS` + `PERMISSION_CATALOG` + defaults + nav/API gates in the same change.
